{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"e6d4813f22ddb02ab4ff047e0d9770a56e42fd25"},"timestamp":1534198912,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzNTAyMTQ5MDM=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2768","origin":"github"},"title":"Option to wait on running transfer when issuing a datalad get on the same file many times","message":"#### What is the problem?\nIn certain situations, we may call `datalad get` on the same file many times. Currently, when requesting the file content a second time, the following error is thrown:\n```bash\nTotal (0 ok, 1 failed out of 1):   0%| | 0.00/61.5M [00:00\u003c?, ?B/s][WARNING] Running get resulted in stderr output: git-annex: get: 1 failed\n \n                                                                      [ERROR  ] transfer already in progress, or unable to take transfer lock; Unable to access these remotes: google; Try making some of these repositories available:; \t9b7e766e-eecb-4cc9-a893-cb6329d1fe1b -- [google]; ; (Note that these git remotes have annex-ignore set: github) [get(/home/simon/Documents/carmin-server/data/admin/test82/9.txt)] \nget(error): /home/simon/Documents/carmin-server/data/admin/test82/9.txt (file) [transfer already in progress, or unable to take transfer lock; Unable to access these remotes: google; Try making some of these repositories available:; \t9b7e766e-eecb-4cc9-a893-cb6329d1fe1b -- [google]; ; (Note that these git remotes have annex-ignore set: github)]\n```\nNote: The error was formatted this way in my terminal.\n\nI looked at the Datalad documentation and didn't find any option that would, when calling `datalad get` on a given file another time, wait for the first `get` operation to complete and then exit normally. Such an option would solve some of the possible issues our platform could encounter through its usage of Datalad. (Please ping @glatard if further information is needed)  \n \n#### What steps will reproduce the problem?\n1. Publish a large file to a remote sibling.\n3. Drop the large file.\n2. Perform 2 concurrent `get` operations of the large file.\n\n#### What version of DataLad are you using?\nDatalad: datalad 0.10.1\nOS: Ubuntu 18.04.1 LTS\nRemotes: Github with a dependency to Google Drive\n\n#### Have you had any success using DataLad before?\nI have been using Datalad a lot throughout the last 7 weeks and I really enjoyed my experience. It was very challenging at first due to the particular use cases I had and the technological stack that git-annex and Datalad both represent for newcomers, but very straight forward and easy to use once the workflow is understood.","files":null}]}